## Random-enchant jackpot is BiS

Rank a random-enchant green on the **best suffix it can roll** (top of that suffix’s range), not the expected value across every suffix.

- Superior Shoulders of Agility at 22 is **+6–7 Agi** (~9.5%). If that roll would be #1 in the slot, it **must** appear as BiS #1.
- `suffixChance` / the log hint tell the player the roll is slim. Chance never buries the hunt.
- Implemented in `pipeline/scripts/score.py` `best_variant` (`ROLL_POLICY="bestRoll"` ranks on jackpot).

## Leveling survivability (through 60)

Leveling is not raid min-max. Stamina, health, and armor beat a naked +1 primary-stat upgrade. Level 60 uses the same multipliers. Hit, crit, and weapon damage stay on the raw weights.

- Example: at 22, **Brawler’s / Trapper’s Leather Tunic** (8 Agi + stam / str / int) beat **Panther Armor** (9 Agi, no stam).
- `score.py` `weights_at_level()` multiplies sta / health / hp5 ×3 and armor ×2 when `level <= 60`.

## Leveling endurance (through 60)

Survivability also means having and keeping mana. Call this **endurance**. It is less important than stamina, but it matters for most classes (paladin seals/heals, shaman shocks, hunter shots, caster drinks).

- `weights_at_level()` multiplies int / spirit / mp5 / mana ×2 when `level <= 60` (stam is ×3).
- At 60, a stored hit, crit, dodge, or parry is dropped when it is only the old rating conversion of a percent line (2% hit stored as 20, 1% crit as 14, 1% dodge as 12, 1% parry as 15). The other percent lines were never stored, and copying that scale onto them put a 3% hit sword above Grand Marshal's Polearm. A Use amount stored as passive attack power, with no Equip line, is not scored twice. The mana-while-casting relic conversion (Polished Driftwood Icon) is halved against the raw weights at 60, so Totem of the Storm and Totem of Life lead that slot. Forever level-60 guides may pin later; until then `GQ_NO_GUIDES=1`.

## Warrior tank is physical

Warrior Protection does not score spell power or healing. A glove with +SP / +healing (Silvered Gauntlets) ranks on the stamina, armor, and defense it actually has, in the same list as every other piece.

## Shaman Enhancement Tank is a hybrid

Like paladin Protection: 1h + shield, stamina/armor/defense first, then Rockbiter melee threat, then Earth Shock / Lightning Shield spell threat. Not dual-wield (Forever has no shaman DW). `enhancement_tank` in `weights.json`.

## Refreshed Forever tooltips (score from these)

Stored item facts must match the refreshed Wowhead Forever tooltip before a score. `refresh_forever_tips.py` writes those facts, then re-score. Do not score a row that still disagrees with the tooltip. Do not full-ingest to refresh tips (that replaces `sources.json` for id ≥ 200000). The 10 Oct 2026 dataEnv 16 pass is the current refresh, and all nine classes were re-scored from it. The 7 Oct pass (1186 items) is the one before that. Quest lookup after that pass moved Medal of Courage (6723) to 35 and five Zandalar pieces to 58 (19846, 19848, 19849, 20033, 20034). It also lowered the level-60 dungeon sets to 58; those were restored and stay locked in `DUNGEON_SET_60`. Do not run that lookup in a way that lowers them again. Client pins stay: Coldflame, Silverlaine, Wolfsbane required level 20. Kaleidoscope resist 5 stays. Emit the audit **before** rescoring so recovered ids leave `FOREVER_MISSING`.

- The Equip line `Increases damage and healing done by magical spells and effects by up to N` is stored as **both** heal=N and damageDone=N. Do not strip it. Do not collapse it to spell power only. `forever_stats` folds damageDone into spell power so it is not counted twice. Holy uses the heal half. Mages (heal weight 0) use the damage half. An unequal "healing up to X and damage up to Y" stays heal=X, damageDone=Y (Staff of Westfall: 48 and 16). Skip party lines. A green `+N Spell Power` line is spell power only.
- **Required level is the tooltip `Requires Level`, never item level.** A stated level greater than 1 is never replaced. Fang of Magmatus is 13. Every item with **no** required level (or Wowhead's stub of 1) is assumed to be a quest reward, or some other gated source, until looked up. Find the quest on Wowhead Forever and set the required level to the **minimum** level that can pick up that quest (`Requires level N`; item XML `<json>` reqlevel, not `jsonEquip`, not the scaling minLevel). Several quests: take the lowest. A chain of at least five steps that must enter a dungeon uses that step's quest level when it is at least 8 levels above the pickup. Final Passage (Windstorm Hammer 6804, Dancing Flame 6806) is 36 because Test of Lore in Scarlet Monastery Library is level 36. Mage's Wand (7513, 7514, 11263) is 40 because Rituals of Power is level 40. Confront Yeh'kinya (20218, 20219) is 58. Drakefire Amulet (16309) is 60. Leaders of the Fang stays 10. The Defias Brotherhood stays 14. The item-level floor is only a stand-in until that lookup is done. Fang is not pinned over Golemheart.
- Cloaks, rings, necks, trinkets, and held items with `kind` `?` are `Misc`. `kind` `?` is not equippable.
- Weapon headers are labels only. For a priest, a mage, a warlock, a balance or restoration druid, and elemental or restoration, a one-hand weapon is ranked as that weapon plus the best off-hand in the current band. A staff stays scored alone. The one-hand rank line names that off-hand. The stored score, the green arrow, and the off-hand list stay the piece by itself. If a staff is rank 1, main-hand rank 2 is the one-hand that off-hand rank 1 pairs with. A second staff may sit at rank 3 with a higher score than rank 2.
- Fishing and skinning are Profession. A crafted hunt states the Forever recipe skill on the line just before Source. A quest reward states `This quest can be picked up at level N.` on the line just before Source. That line is green at or above N and red below N. The next line is `Recommended to pick this quest up at level M.` M is the item level minus 4, the same wait as Manageable Quests, and it stops at 60. When that quest cannot be picked up until a higher level, M is that pickup level. Replica Crescent Necklace recommends 25 because that quest cannot be picked up until 25. A missing item level skips that line. It uses the same green and red. A chain lists every Wowhead series step from the first quest through the quest that rewards the item. A quest whose Wowhead series is only that quest says No prequests. You can pick this quest up without finishing another quest first. A quest that has not been checked stays quiet. An unfinished step ends with `- not completed yet`. A finished step ends with `- completed` in green. A PvP rank purchase states the required rank (`Requires Sergeant (Rank 3).`). The price uses the coin icons, and honor or mark icons when Wowhead lists those. A stored reputation requirement is shown for every source. Onyxia's Lair drops say the lair requires the Drakefire Amulet. The description names the seller Wowhead lists. Sergeant's Cloak is Sergeant Ba'sha in Orgrimmar. Sergeant's Cape is Officer Areyn in Stormwind. N is the stored required level. The hunt list shows `#N` in faded grey in the collapse-icon column on every hunt row. That column is wide enough for `#99`, and a single digit stays centered in it so `#9` and `#10` keep the item names in one line. N is that piece's place on the rank tooltip for the slot, including `#4` and later when an earlier piece was already obtained. A faction hole closes up, so the list number matches the tooltip. Each hunt row is two lines tall, with a small gap before the next hunt. The gear icon is 28 pixels and sits beside both lines. The first line is the item name, and Recommended sits after that name. The second line is the smaller rank font. It holds New at this level, or Since level N when the hunt was already on the list. N is the first level of the current run where that piece's rank was inside Hunts per gear slot. (Set piece), (Guide), and (Tracked) stay on that second line. A question mark stands in until the client has the icon. Slot headers stay the plus and minus. The skill clause is green when the character meets the recipe and red when they are short or do not have the profession. The description does not repeat it: strip `Crafted with Leatherworking (requires skill N).` and list recipe materials there (`Materials: Light Leather (8), Coarse Thread (4).`) from the Wowhead Forever spell tooltip via `fetch_craft_skills.py --reagents`. Every new profession hunt, and every update of an existing profession hunt, looks that skill up in the same pass: ForeverDB `made` on `crafting/{id % 64}.json`, confirmed on the Wowhead Forever spell page (`Requires Leatherworking (40)`) when Wowhead is up. The item tooltip does not carry it. Run `fetch_craft_skills.py`. A skill of 1 is real when both say 1. Do not invent 1. Dress Shoes (6836) has no recipe. Container loot uses the Container filter. Boss drop has a dungeon flyout for the dungeons that have a boss-drop hunt at the current level, including lower ranks. Dungeon & Raid trash has the same flyout for trash hunts at the current level, and those boxes are separate from Boss drop. Hall of Thanes, Ruins of Lordaeron, and Excavation Site are on that list. Other is bosses that are not in a dungeon or raid. The flyouts do not scroll. Select all / Deselect all on the filter menu covers the source list and the profession, boss, trash, and vendor sub-filters. Each of those flyouts has the same button, and it covers only the boxes on that flyout. The parchment reward name uses the item rarity color. The box beside the icon shows the full name. It widens up to the parchment, and a longer name wraps onto another line instead of ending in an ellipsis. Vendor opens Reputation, Honor (PvP), and Ordinary. Ordinary is a purchase with no faction standing and no honor cost. Honor is a battleground, arena, or PvP rank purchase, including Arathi standing. A town vendor who also sells one rank-named piece stays Ordinary for the rest. Thrallmar and Honor Hold stay Reputation. A vendor piece that needs both standing and honor hides when either of those boxes is off. Unchecking Vendor hides every vendor piece. Play style sits at the bottom of the log. Seven cards, names under the pictures, three then three, then Focus Zone under Manageable Dungeons. Focus Zone keeps a hunt only when the zone the character is standing in is that hunt's zone or one of its spots. Quests, vendors, crafts, world drops, and dungeon drops all follow. A hunt with no place stays hidden. Changing zone keeps the current rows and builds the new zone one slot per frame, with an idle frame between slots, then swaps the list once. The green upgrade arrow is on both lists. It stays on the unfiltered best pieces when a filter or a play style hides them, and it stays on every hunt still showing, including a later rank, a notable, or a tracked hunt. Get it now can be on with either dungeon card, and with Manageable Dungeons, Manageable Quests, Buy it, and Focus Zone. No Dungeons and Dungeon Enjoyer turn each other off. Manageable Dungeons hides a boss drop, and dungeon and raid trash, until the level being viewed reaches 4 under that item's level. The wait stops at 60, so a level 60 drop stays even when its item level is higher. A missing item level stays. Quests, vendors, crafts, and world drops stay. Manageable Quests hides a quest reward until the level being viewed reaches 4 under that item's level. When the quest cannot be picked up until a higher level, the wait uses that pickup level. The wait stops at 60, so a level 60 reward