## Mage Battle Mage

Caster who swings. Specs: `battlemage_frost` (the hunt), `battlemage_fire`, `battlemage_arcane`. Spell power of that school first. Stamina base 0.15 (slightly above frost 0.1). Weapon `dpsWeight` 0.35. Coldflame Saber and Blade of Silverlaine stats stay pinned in `client_item_overrides.json` (10.9 and 12.2 DPS, the spell bonus, required level 21). The hover is the dataEnv 16 page: one Equip line for that bonus, not two green +Spell Power and +Healing Done lines. Do not sync an older nether damage line back over the pin. The saber’s 98 Fire vs Frozen is every swing during a freeze (`FROZEN_MELEE_UPTIME` 25% frost, 15% fire/arcane). On an imbued weapon, printed stats stay the normal colors and only the imbue effect is grey. Do not repeat that effect. Add `Use: Combine the <base weapon> and <scroll>.` (`CLIENT_IMBUE` in `Data.lua`).

## GearQuest score (display only)

Hunt order stays `pipelineScore`. Do not call `GetItemInfo` while building the hover score, and cache `GetSlotRankList` plus `GearScoreContext` for the current level, spec, and equipped items. A scan must not call `GetItemInfo` for an item the client has not already cached. While item priming is suppressed, `IsItemDataCached` returns false instead of calling `GetItemInfo`, and `GetEquipSlot` and `GetItemArmorSubclass` return before `GetItemInfo` when the item is not cached. The score cache keeps every slot scored for this level, spec, and gear, so moving across a bag and back does not rebuild a slot. The score bar still must not call `GearScoreContext` once per slot. It uses `GearScoreWornRows` and `WornSlotIndex`. The obtain toast does not use this scan. It compares the looted item id to the hunt on the list. The tooltip index is display-only: best raw score in the slot at this level is **100**, worst is **0** (`GearScoreIndex`). Do not retune weights so the index matches the rank, and do not store the index on a pick. The line sits inside the item tooltip (hunt hover, character panel, chat, quest log) and on each (i) rank-list row. It is not on hunt-list rows. **General -> GearQuest score on tooltips** (`settings.showGearScore`, on when nil). Green `GQ-ArrowUp.png` / red `GQ-ArrowDown.png` compare to the equipped piece. Empty slot: index only. Rings and trinkets compare to the weaker piece only when both slots are filled. A worn piece that aged out of the band still compares (`EquippedPipelineScore`, nearest same-spec/faction band). Chat rank uses the active band, not `LEVEL_GRACE` (`EntryForItemLink`). **Kodohide Legguards** (285338) is rank 4 for Enhancement Horde at 25-27. **Pathfinder Belt** ranks only **of the Falcon**. If the piece is gear and not that ranked row, `GearScoreMissText` says why (suffix, level range, spec, class, faction, or no score). Hunts -> Recommended gear enchantment (settings.showGearEnchant) is off until the player turns it on. The gear tooltip adds one line immediately above the rank line. Only the words Recommended enchantment are yellow. The rest is white: the formula name, then the effect. The formula is the best one this level can reach for the spec on screen. Enchanting formulas, armor kits, and scopes are for every character. The level decides how high a formula is in reach, and a kit or a scope also keeps its own required level. Wowhead Forever does not list a tailoring embroidery, an enchanter-only ring enchant, or any other worn effect that says only one profession can wear it. Until a spell says that, nothing is hidden for lack of a profession. The formula's required level, and the item level a kit can be used on, still apply. Armor on an enchant counts for a tank only. Every other spec scores that enchant's other stats and ignores its armor. Flat stats otherwise use the same weights as the hunt. A weapon proc is a judgment of what the effect does. Insight is the healer proc, Revelation is the caster proc, and Crusader and Grand Crusader are the melee procs. A scope is only a bow, a gun, or a crossbow. The client names those Bows, Guns, and Crossbows. A wand and a thrown weapon get no line. Enchant Cloak - Defense is +30 Armor, Greater Defense is +60, and Superior Defense is +70. Mystic Rugged Armor Kit is +6 Spell Power and +40 Armor at level 50. The enchant line uses GetItemInfoInstant and does not call GetItemInfo on an id the client has not already cached. Rebuilding a tooltip clears the enchant flag with the rank flag. Bags, quivers, and ammo are skipped. Simulation shows **Turn off simulation mode to see your GearQuest Score for this item.** The Simulator button says **Turn off simulation**. A `setPiece` at `curatedRank` 1 whose stored score is below another piece in the slot adds **Rank 1 when you wear multiple pieces of this set.** Enhancement Horde 25-27: **Leggings of the Fang** (10410) rank 1 score 20.87; **Triprunner Dungarees** (9624) rank 2 score 21.56. Fang stays rank 1. Do not change `apply_embrace_package`. On the active hunt list, a slot header whose rank #1 the character already has (obtained, or worn) reads **- Rank #1 BiS acquired** after that header's (i). Among rank #1 pieces the character does not have, the three largest GearQuest score gains versus what is worn are marked **Recommended** after the item name, each with its own (i): "One of the best upgrades for your level. GearQuest marks up to three rank #1 pieces, the ones that improve what you are wearing the most." An empty slot is that piece's raw pipeline score, not an index jump from 0 to 100. It is recommended only when that score beats the raw gain of a rank #1 piece in a slot that already has gear. A downgrade is not recommended. A later rank is never the recommendation. Simulation hides both. Turning the score off hides the recommendation and leaves the acquired line. When you are not simulating, the log header is a four-section GearQuest score bar (average equipped index on that same 0–100 scale, empty slots show 0 and “(empty slot)”, clamped 0–100, 25 points a section, green then blue then purple then orange) with white “GearQuest Index Score - Collecting feedback on this” above it. Hover reads N / 100 · Below average (green), Fair (blue), Great (epic), or Legend (orange). Simulation keeps its header sentence. **General -> GearQuest score bar** (`settings.showGearScoreBar`, on when nil). Off hides the bar and shows the viewing-upgrades sentence. Equipping or removing gear refreshes the bar. The weapon filter does not move the bar. The main-hand index uses the whole main-hand list. The Weapons (i) list uses one scale for both hands, and each arrow compares to the hand that weapon is worn in. **General -> Hide chat messages** (`settings.hideChat`, off when nil) stops every GearQuest line in chat, including login, obtain notices, errors, and `/gq` replies. The log, tooltips, toasts, and score bar stay. The General page scrolls. The Hide chat messages box reads the saved check when Settings is shown and writes it on the next frame.

The **Play style** button reads **Play style*** while any play style is on.

A ding, a zone change, and a cold log stay off the single frame that used to hitch. Level up warms the query cache one slot per frame, with an idle frame between slots (WarmQueryCacheAsync gap 1). Milestones, the obtain check, and the redraw each wait a frame. Paper-doll arrows on a ding are one slot per frame. The previous-level new probe idles between slots. Changing zone, logging in, and opening a merchant rebuild arrows into side tables and swap them in when the pass finishes, so the old arrows stay until then. Opening the log, a filter, or the Active tab, when rank lists are not ready, keeps the current rows and swaps the list once (ScheduleRankListWarm). Completed and Removed do not wait. A warm list stays instant. Tooltip hovers and a Simulator class switch stay on the frame they already used. Do not slice those.

With the mouse UI, map pins are frames on the canvas placed by the pin mixin, so they stay on the spot when the map zooms. Do not `AddDataProvider`, do not write `WorldMapFrame.pinPools`, do not hook `WorldMapFrame` OnShow, and do not `Hide()` a pin during the map's hide. That path taints `SetPreferredGamepadInteractTarget`. While the gamepad UI is on, the canvas gets no frames at all. Show on map and the guide still set the Blizzard user waypoint. The world-drop icon is `GQ-WorldDrop.png`. While the log is open and GearQuest is the window being used, the pad shows a gold chevron (a smaller arrow inside a larger one) to the left of the focused control and a blue highlight on it. The chevron eases toward that control. The window gets a soft gold glow that follows the portrait ring. A click on a hunt or another control moves that arrow onto it. LB sits above the side handles and RB below them. A dark bar under the window reads A Select, Y Filters, Navigate, and B Close, and an open menu gets A Select, Navigate, and B Close under it. Opening a Blizzard window while GearQuest has the pad gives that window the pad, and these marks hide. A click anywhere on GearQuest takes the pad back. Read FrameControlsManager.currentFrame only. Do not call its methods. On the hunt list the arrows and the left stick move through the hunts and skip the filters. Down moves to the next hunt. Up from the top hunt reaches Active, Completed, and Removed. Left and right move among those tabs. Down from a tab returns to the first hunt. Y moves the arrow onto the filter controls and does not change the list. A second Y returns to the hunts. A on a filter control opens it. The bottom face button confirms, and moving onto a checkbox does not change it. After a hunt is selected with A, the arrow moves to Track. The d-pad and the left stick then move among Track, Show on map, and Remove, and back to the hunts. The right stick scrolls the parchment. While the character panel's paper doll is open and the log does not own the pad, clicking the right stick opens the upgrade list for the focused slot, or the slot last hovered when the pad focus is not a slot. The same click closes that list when it is already open for that slot. The bumpers do not change those tabs. The left bumper goes to the previous page and the right bumper to the next, wrapping. The level box and the search box open the on-screen keyboard. While that box has focus, the pad belongs to the keyboard, and B leaves the box. The right face button closes a menu, then the filters, then the log. Button names come from the mapped pad state, lined up so the bottom face button is confirm and the right face button is back. The raw state only fills a bumper the mapped state left out. One press is one action. A direction does not also confirm or close. Up and down on Settings and the other pages walk the next control in that column and stop at the ends. Left and right move only when a control sits that way. Closing Play Style, the source filter, or the weapon menu clears the highlight. Do not treat Ctrl as the left bumper, and do not relabel a direction as Jump. Do not call FrameControlsManager methods. Do not walk UIParent children. Do not call SetUIFocusState. The highlight ticks only while that log is open. Mouse mode does not start it. Closing the log stops it.

Dungeon upgrade sets are level **60** quests, not level 1. Classic Feralheart, Beastmaster, Heroism, The Five Thunders, Darkmantle, Deathmist, Soulforge, Virtuous, and Sorcerer's (72) plus the Forever spec copies (144) are those quests at gate 60, `questRaces` 0. Wrists: An Earnest Proposition. Hands and waist: Just Compensation. Feet, legs, shoulders: Anthion's Parting Words. Head and chest: Saving the Best for Last. The pin is the chain start, An Earnest Proposition. Those pieces stay locked at required level 60 in `DUNGEON_SET_60`. A quest lookup must not lower them to 58. Medal of Courage (6723) is 35. Zandalar Illusionist's Wraps (19846), Demoniac's Wraps (19848), Demoniac's Mantle (19849), Demoniac's Robe (20033), and Illusionist's Robe (20034) are 58. Leave out Beaststalker, Beastmaster's Girdle (5355), Darkmoon Card: Heroism, Uncle's Heroism, Violet Sorcerer's, Ogre Sorcerer Belt, and Sorcerer Collar. No quest and item level 15 or below, with no real Requires Level, is wearable at 1.

